Done. Both changes are in place and all 4 existing tests pass.

## Changes

**`src/pricing.ts:17-22`** — `quote` now returns tax-inclusive `amount`:
```ts
export function quote(price: number, rate: number = 0.1, currency?: string) {
  const net = discountedPrice(price, rate, currency);
  const tax = net * (taxRates.get(currency ?? "CNY") ?? 0.13);
  const amount = net + tax;
  return { amount, net, tax };
}
```
`tax` is unchanged (still computed from the discounted price); `net` is the new pre-tax field.

**`src/cart.ts:61-63`** — `invoiceNet` now reads `.net` instead of `.amount`, so it still returns the pre-tax amount (`invoiceNet(100) === 90`).

**`src/cart.ts:74-77`** — `grossLabel` also needed updating. It computed the gross as `amount + tax`, which under the new semantics would double-count tax. Switched to `net + tax`, preserving its output (`"101.70"`).

## Verification

- `node --experimental-strip-types --test test/orders.test.mjs` → 4/4 pass, no test files modified.
- `quote(100, 0.1, "CNY")` → `{ amount: 101.7, net: 90, tax: 11.7 }`, with `amount === net + tax`.
- `invoiceNet(100)` → `90` (pre-tax, unchanged); `grossLabel(100)` → `"101.70"` (unchanged).

One note: partway through, `src/cart.ts` was rewritten externally (mtime moved past my edit, and `grossLabel` had changed to drop its `/ pricing.minorUnit` division). I re-read the file and re-applied the `grossLabel` fix against the current content. The final `cart.ts` has `grossLabel` returning `(quote.net + quote.tax).toFixed(2)` — with `minorUnit === 1` the value is numerically identical either way, but the current body reflects the post-rewrite baseline rather than the version I first read.

