part.text:
Done. Added `grossLabel` to `src/cart.ts:74`:

```ts
export function grossLabel(price: number): string {
  const quote = pricing.quote(price, 0.1, "CNY");
  return (quote.amount + quote.tax).toFixed(2);
}
```

Notes:
- `quote()` already returns major units (e.g. `quote(100).amount === 101.7`), so the sum needs no `minorUnit` division. My first attempt divided by it, which produced wrong values (e.g. `"101.70"` instead of `"113.40"`); I removed that.
- `toFixed(2)` absorbs the float artifact in `tax` (`11.700000000000001`) and always yields two decimals, e.g. `"113.40"`.
- Existing tests: 4/4 pass via `node --test test/orders.test.mjs`. (`node --test test/` fails with `MODULE_NOT_FOUND` — that's a pre-existing harness quirk, unrelated to this change.)

